# The public registry is the committed default, which is what keeps this repo
# buildable by anyone who clones it.
#
# This file exists because of how `npm ci` treats the lockfile. npm rewrites a
# `resolved` URL that points at the *default* registry to whatever registry is
# configured — so a lockfile resolved against registry.npmjs.org installs fine
# from a private mirror. It does **not** rewrite in the other direction: a
# lockfile carrying a private mirror's URL makes `npm ci` request that host no
# matter what registry is configured, and an outside clone fails with ENOTFOUND
# on every package.
#
# A project .npmrc beats a user one, so this pins lockfile writes to the public
# registry even on a machine whose ~/.npmrc defaults to the on-prem Verdaccio.
# Without it, the next `npm install` on the LAN quietly re-poisons the lockfile
# and the public build breaks again.
#
# Environment variables beat *this* file, which is what leaves the private path
# intact: Kaniko injects NPM_CONFIG_REGISTRY and the container build goes to
# Verdaccio, using this same lockfile.
registry=https://registry.npmjs.org/
